    "narrative": "The offensive engine for LawDog today centers on high-upside matchups against favorable arms, with **Lawrence Butler** (69.61) and **Cal Raleigh** (69.52) leading the charge. **Lawrence Butler** is our strongest play, benefiting from a high base projection and a +13% platoon edge against Ure\u00f1a, while **Cal Raleigh** leverages his favorable #3 spot in the order against Cantillo to secure elite daily status. The most significant boosts for the squad come from the matchup against L\u00f3pez, R, where **Luis Arraez**, **Matt Chapman**, and **Jung Hoo Lee** all see their scores elevated by a substantial +19% SP skill adjustment and a +5% wind-out factor. **Luis Arraez** in particular is positioned perfectly in the leadoff spot to capitalize on these conditions, making him a cornerstone for our AVG and run-scoring potential.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the card was keeping **Gavin Sheets** (57.47) just outside the top-tier, as he narrowly missed the 60+ threshold despite a positive SP skill adjustment against Sasaki. He remains a viable utility option, but he is held back by a slight park penalty that kept his score marginally lower than the likes of **Geraldo Perdomo** (60.17) and **Yainer Diaz** (60.15). We are closely monitoring the status of **Masyn Winn** (43.34), who carries the lowest score of the active starters; his value is suppressed by a negative SP skill adjustment against Meyer and the general scarcity of stolen bases, though we remain committed to his roster spot for his speed profile. With **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** and **Will Smith** sidelined on the IL, and **Tyler Freeman** and **Ryan Waldschmidt** unavailable, our depth is thin, placing a premium on the performance of **Daulton Varsho** (51.12), whose score is tempered by Eovaldi\u2019s ability to suppress baserunners. No major weather warnings are currently impacting the board, but the reliance on favorable wind in the L\u00f3pez, R start is a key variable to track as first pitch approaches.",
